.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel/

# local owner-review artifacts (screenshots, static review HTML) — never committed
/runtime/
/apps/web/runtime/

# LIVE BROWSER PROFILES — security audit finding M-06.
#
# runtime/auth/ holds real Chrome profiles with the owner's logged-in session
# (cookies, tokens, Local State). `/runtime/` above already covers them, BUT the
# working convention in this repo is `git add -f` under runtime/ so that
# runtime/audits/*.md can be tracked despite the blanket ignore — and `git add -f`
# bypasses EVERY ignore rule, including this one. One careless `git add -f
# runtime/` would publish live owner sessions to a PUBLIC repository.
#
# These entries are intent + defence in depth. The ENFORCEABLE control is
# apps/web/lib/guards/no-tracked-browser-profiles.test.ts, which fails CI if any
# such file ever becomes tracked. Ignore rules alone cannot stop `-f`.
/runtime/auth/
**/chrome-debug/
**/owner-chrome-profile/

# playwright / e2e local artifacts (never committed)
#
# The glob is the actual guarantee. Every entry below it was added one at a
# time as someone invented a new suffix, which only protects the variants
# already thought of: the beta foundation audit (2026-08-09) minted
# `.storage-state-worker.json` and `.storage-state-employer.json` — real
# session tokens, one `git add -A` away from being committed, because the
# dash spelling matched none of the dot-spelled lines. Any file whose name
# starts with `.storage-state` holds a session and is ignored from here on.
#
# THAT WAS STILL AN ENUMERATION, AND IT FAILED A SECOND TIME (2026-08-09).
# The rule above pins a PREFIX, so the mobile sweep's `.company-state.json`
# — a real `sb-127-auth-token` cookie — was committable again. Twice now the
# fix has been "add the spelling we just met" and twice the next spelling
# walked past it. The pattern below describes the CLASS instead: any JSON in
# the e2e directory with `state` in its name is a session artefact and is
# ignored, whatever anyone calls it next. A committed session token cannot be
# un-leaked by deleting the file afterwards, so this errs toward over-ignoring
# — an e2e fixture that genuinely needs committing can be force-added.
/apps/web/tests/e2e/*state*.json
/apps/web/tests/e2e/.storage-state*.json
/apps/web/tests/e2e/.storage-state.json
/apps/web/tests/e2e/.storage-state.company.json
/apps/web/tests/e2e/.storage-state.worker.json
# The PRODUCTION QA session. Holds a real access token for the synthetic QA
# identity — it must never be committed, attached to a report, or shipped
# inside a trace. Minted per run by scripts/prod-qa-mint-session.ts.
/apps/web/tests/e2e/.storage-state.prod-qa.json
/apps/web/test-results/
/apps/web/playwright-report/

# owner visual-proof capture (holds a live Google login session + authed
# screenshots — never committed; see scripts/capture-ia-proof.mjs)
/apps/web/.playwright-ia-proof-profile/
/apps/web/.playwright-proofs/
/apps/web/ia-proof/

# local research/proof artifacts (playwright CLI logs, ad-hoc run output).
# The auto-commit workflow stages with `git add .`; without these entries a
# session's 79MB of local artifacts is one commit away from landing on main.
/.playwright-cli/
/output/
/apps/output/
/apps/web/output/

